"location_name_detailed": "Harrogate, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-11-08", "published_at_date": "2018-11-08"}, {"review_id": 631814927, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r631814927-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Into the Lord's lap", "text": "We were destined to meet the Lord Pashupatinath that evening.The temple closes down at 7 pm, and we reached there at 7.10 pm. There was a motley crowd and people were being asked to leave the temple premises. Do not know why, the guard asked us to hurry and visit the Lord, before He went into rest. Words fail me in describing the satisfaction that we got after \"meeting\" the Pashupatinath. The temple is very clean and was well lighted. We also got to witness the aarti across the river, from the ramparts of the temple. What else could we ask for ?", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "1E214E37EC9D410FE2DDE8DA0FEFFA1F", "name": "Pratik_Priya", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Pratik_Priya", "username": "Pratik_Priya", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/14/6f/45/6f/pratik-priya.jpg", "contribution_count": 109, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304551, "location_name": "New Delhi", "location_name_detailed": "New Delhi, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-11-08", "published_at_date": "2018-11-08"}, {"review_id": 631814205, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r631814205-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "For me the best site in Kathmandu", "text": "We did a 4 stop tour in Kathmandu and for me this was the best one. Although lots of earthquake damage still exists it’s one of the places where it still feels very connected to the Hindu religion and not be over run with tourist traps and shops. \n\nThere were a few cremation ceremonies whilst we were there which was very interesting to watch. Get a guide you can explain to you what’s what as there is very little in the way of information or directions inside. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2018-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "5237E3ECDEE6D605E6DEB45239ACBD3B", "name": "NikanV", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/NikanV", "username": "NikanV", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/17/1a/bd/17/nikanv.jpg", "contribution_count": 47, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255060, "location_name": "Sydney", "location_name_detailed": "Sydney, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-11-08", "published_at_date": "2018-11-08"}, {"review_id": 631593460, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r631593460-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Must Visit", "text": "Hindu only temple of lord Shiva. Not a Jyotirlinga but of same importance. Try sitting on the platform of the temple at the backside near the bank od river. You will feel just peace.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2018-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "314626ABD60A4E7809682D0BD45E8733", "name": "amitmaihar", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/amitmaihar", "username": "amitmaihar", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ee/10/default-avatar-2020-8.jpg", "contribution_count": 14, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 3395996, "location_name": "Maihar", "location_name_detailed": "Maihar, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-11-07", "published_at_date": "2018-11-07"}, {"review_id": 631577574, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r631577574-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Boom Shankar", "text": "Shiva is calling listen the silence within u.it was a motorcycle trip to nepal and during mooson . one of the divine and sacred land of shiva in land of Buddha.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2018-08-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "687AC2F1A535E6D00836EC9D4DBCDFD1", "name": "Dhirendra Y", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/dhirendray2015", "username": "dhirendray2015", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/15/48/98/f3/dhirendra-y.jpg", "contribution_count": 66, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 297637, "location_name": "Thiruvananthapuram (Trivandrum)", "location_name_detailed": "Thiruvananthapuram (Trivandrum), India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/15/48/a4/0a/boom-shankar.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2018-11-07", "published_at_date": "2018-11-07"}, {"review_id": 631232586, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r631232586-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Fascinating Place", "text": "This is a really interesting place to visit to get some understanding into how the local people manage the last rites of their dead and you may need to be prepared as you will witness the bodies being cremated by the river.  Aside, there are multiple temples,  interesting buildings and monkeys to see.  Definitely a place worth visiting.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2018-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "01DA8348FCE69430D4A92812D3F92E27", "name": "Pete_Gill_W", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Pete_Gill_W", "username": "Pete_Gill_W", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0b/80/eb/e7/pete-gill-w.jpg", "contribution_count": 446, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 186391, "location_name": "Haslemere", "location_name_detailed": "Haslemere, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-11-06", "published_at_date": "2018-11-06"}, {"review_id": 630832098, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r630832098-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A place of faith and worship ", "text": "Lord Shiva’s abode in Himalayas. This temple is a historical place with many generations of Nepali Kings and its people associated with it. It has a great vibration and you instantly feel calm and peace in the temple vicinity. The temple tends to be crowded so be ready for some line. There are local guides though , who can help you take you inside\nwith ease . next to the temple , on the bank of a river one can see Hindu crematorium where last rites are performed as per Hindu religious system. \nBe aware of touts and pick pocketers while visiting. . \n", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "96D055E1B43E3C50461E450E32712AEF", "name": "santosh t", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/485santosht", "username": "485santosht", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1b/07/11/a9/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 261, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304554, "location_name": "Mumbai", "location_name_detailed": "Mumbai, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/15/41/6b/cd/photo0jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/15/41/6b/ce/photo1jpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2018-11-05", "published_at_date": "2018-11-05"}, {"review_id": 630735849, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r630735849-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Sprawling Temple complex but limited access", "text": "If you are not a Hindu then you are not allowed to see the inner part of the temple but can just look from outside. The external part is impressive and the adjacent Cremation Ghats on the banks of Bagmati river can be visited by Non-Hindus. It is a personal choice whether you go to see people being cremated or not. It is a macabre place though. However, there are many smaller temples and these are dedicated to Lord Shiva in the same complex..", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "E6DF7AF522A145917C12C9BCECD5C491", "name": "Eaa1947", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Eaa1947", "username": "Eaa1947", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f1/42/default-avatar-2020-20.jpg", "contribution_count": 801, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255337, "location_name": "Gold Coast", "location_name_detailed": "Gold Coast, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-11-04", "published_at_date": "2018-11-04"}, {"review_id": 630654280, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r630654280-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Little slice of perspective", "text": "As a non hindu you cannot enter the actual temple but can wander the outer grounds. If you go up around the left side you can kind of look down into the courtyard. Behind the temple down a road by the side you can see the cremations. Pretty sobering stuff. Beware the money grubbing babas. They are opportunists, not holy men! A guide also tried to jump me us at the gate with his foreign friendly charm. I shook him off as I prefer to go at my own pace.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "4FAB4B61D1147E7182A086BFADD96081", "name": "the world beater", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/nickjF78", "username": "nickjF78", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/12/1b/13/47/nforbes78.jpg", "contribution_count": 61, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 293936, "location_name": "Dhaka City", "location_name_detailed": "Dhaka City, Bangladesh"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/15/3f/5c/57/20181020-115016-largejpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2018-11-04", "published_at_date": "2018-11-04"}, {"review_id": 629868232, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r629868232-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Impactful on many levels", "text": "While we weren't allowed into the temple itself because we are not Hindu, we were able to walk the grounds.  We were witness to many priestly offerings to worshipers, as well as a couple religious cremations that touched us deeply.  It is definitely a profound experience!", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2018-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "552F3B277B3D7A9166117B5FA0B1FECF", "name": "Stevi S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/sasoles21", "username": "sasoles21", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/eb/a3/default-avatar-2020-38.jpg", "contribution_count": 11, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-10-31", "published_at_date": "2018-10-31"}, {"review_id": 629840625, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r629840625-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Religious visit", "text": "The Temple complex is huge and in the middle of the city. There’s always a rush for the evening Aarti. It’s one of the most revered SHIV temple in Hindi religion. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "9AE1D9054FEB8ABDBE0F3CC60BFAEF3B", "name": "Harshrk", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Harshrk", "username": "Harshrk", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e3/1f/default-avatar-2020-46.jpg", "contribution_count": 397, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304554, "location_name": "Mumbai", "location_name_detailed": "Mumbai, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-10-31", "published_at_date": "2018-10-31"}, {"review_id": 629750027, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r629750027-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Kathmandu Short Visit", "text": "Mr.Keshav Dahal was very accommodating and organized a whistle stop for our short stay. Our guide driver top notch. We would love to return and further explore the wonders of Kathmandu and I’m sure We Will be contacting Dahal to organize any guided trips.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2018-04-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "73083BE1237498C60609CBE78F9059BD", "name": "pavel J", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/926pavelj", "username": "926pavelj", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/de/0a/default-avatar-2020-35.jpg", "contribution_count": 1, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-10-31", "published_at_date": "2018-10-31"}, {"review_id": 629678728, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r629678728-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Funeral pyres", "text": "Preparation for cremation takes place on one side of the bridge and cremation on the other. Son of the deceased spends 13 days, isolated in the temple grounds as a grieving ritual. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2018-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "1E2771E0BFA4B8932D26E8AEEDEC1209", "name": "John W", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/E7885NVjohnw", "username": "E7885NVjohnw", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0a/fa/ee/d3/john-w.jpg", "contribution_count": 210, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 59988, "location_name": "Jackson", "location_name_detailed": "Jackson, Wisconsin"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-10-30", "published_at_date": "2018-10-30"}, {"review_id": 629677855, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r629677855-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "A very holy place", "text": "Its a little creepy if you can't understand the rituals of cremation. Funeral pyres and bodies being prepared for cremation are quite visible, but it is a holy place for saying goodbye to loved ones.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2018-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "1E2771E0BFA4B8932D26E8AEEDEC1209", "name": "John W", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/E7885NVjohnw", "username": "E7885NVjohnw", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0a/fa/ee/d3/john-w.jpg", "contribution_count": 210, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 59988, "location_name": "Jackson", "location_name_detailed": "Jackson, Wisconsin"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-10-30", "published_at_date": "2018-10-30"}, {"review_id": 629523407, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r629523407-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Don't miss it!", "text": "As a USA citizen and resident, I've never seen anything like it.  It is shocking!  The public burial ceremonies were incredible.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2018-02-28"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "1A6F7704D7D2F792AE427F1A07355CD5", "name": "ADavidBailey", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/ADavidBailey", "username": "ADavidBailey", "avatar": null, "contribution_count": 11, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 51191, "location_name": "Bartlesville", "location_name_detailed": "Bartlesville, Oklahoma"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-10-30", "published_at_date": "2018-10-30"}, {"review_id": 629408151, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r629408151-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Probably the most important Hindu-Tempel in Nepal ", "text": "He is like i said already in the title one of the most important Hindu-Temple in Nepal. He is lying a little outside of Kathmandu, near the Boudhanath Stupa. Like a lot of Hindu-Tempels you are as not Hindu not allowed to go inside. But on the other side of the temple you still have a good view. He is also famous for the cremation. We were there on a monday at about lunch time and they were many people there for the cremation. To have an inside look of the Hindu-World this temple is a good start.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "1C0EE0695C5731B98B392DD3B9F46B13", "name": "Roger W", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/TheTraveller_247", "username": "TheTraveller_247", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/0f/34/be/2c/roger-w.jpg", "contribution_count": 2066, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 4472752, "location_name": "Siebnen", "location_name_detailed": "Siebnen, Switzerland"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "crea